WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:42.860
Hey Dad, can I eat the candy Grandma gave me?

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.890
No snacks before bedtime, remember?

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.070
Aw, come on... Just one?

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.320
No means no.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.620
Come on, Dad, please!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.680
Don't tell your mother, okay?

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.980
Yay!

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.320
Dad, I think I just saw something...

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.220
Oh yeah... There are a lot 
of deer around these parts.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.950
Or maybe it's a... monster?

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.400
There's nothing to worry 
about! Dad's here, right?

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.030
If a monster appears, then you'll beat it up?

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.410
You got that right!

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.130
A monster or two ain't nothing 
for me to handle.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.240
Papa...

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.800
It's okay. It'll be okay...

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.670
Stay in the car.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.510
Got it?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.600
I'm pretty sure someone was here...

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.030
Dad!

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.800
Oh sure, this is <i>so</i> how I 
want to spend my weekend...

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:17.340
All us guys getting together 
for some gardening?

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:21.840
He only said we were going for a 
drive! He totally tricked us...

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.300
The clear blue sky, the wide open land, the 
sweat dripping from your foreheads...

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.870
I think this is the perfect way 
for youth to spend their weekend.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.370
Easy for you to say!

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.310
What are you researching this time?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.780
Why are we collecting soil samples?

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.650
Do you know about the abductions that 
have been happening in Center City?

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.970
Abductions?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.810
Over the past month a ton of animals,

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:51.270
have been attacked and gone missing,
from cows to horses and even pet dogs.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:57.120
At this point, no clues or motive have 
been discovered about who's responsible.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.460
Why would someone attack animals?

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.670
Some people are just cruel like that.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:06.010
But this time, it's people 
that've gone missing.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.140
Five people in a row.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.140
A man disappeared three days ago 
after a strange car accident.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:16.400
Riiight around here...

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.830
So what does this incident 
have to do with the soil?

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:24.590
That soil is an important witness.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.970
It just might tell us who the culprit is.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:28.370
Huh?

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.300
It's already been three days 
since it happened, right?

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:37.110
Even if there is some evidence left, the 
wind would have carried it away somewhere.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.140
What did you just say?

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.030
You just said "carried away," didn't you?

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.880
That's it! That's what connects everything!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.480
Hurry up and get in!

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:59.030
We've got to do one more 
place before the sun sets!

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.920
If we take a detour I'll be late for work!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.330
So will I!

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.070
Then you guys are on your own!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.450
S-So, we're walking back?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.420
What a jerk!

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.110
It sounds like some sort of joke,

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.300
but I'm tellin' the truth, for real!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:27.950
He couldn't even go to the bathroom 
by himself at night until he was 9!

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:32.310
I tried kicking the door once, 
and he was so scared he fainted!

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.340
Isn't it hilarious?

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.280
Don't know who he takes after, but 
he's like a teensy-weensy acorn!

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.170
<i>An acorn?</i>

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.690
Yeah, a tiny one!

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.790
Tiny Joey and his tiny courage!

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:45.260
Who are you talking to, Sis?

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.460
Some pretty blond what's-her-name...

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:51.360
Hey!

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.830
Hello, Lina?

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.770
<i>Sorry for calling you so late.</i>

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:59.120
<i>Your sister was telling me
a lot about you, Joey.</i>

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.280
No, no! That was our neighborhood drunk!

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.000
I'm sober, damn it!

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.610
Why are you getting in 
the way? Get outta here!

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.420
I'm being serious, man.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:12.850
There ain't even fairy tales about 
acorns gettin' cheerleaders.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.210
I'm sorry, Lina...

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.350
<i>I'm okay.</i>

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.860
<i>You weren't at school, so I was 
worried. Did something happen?</i>

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.570
Well...

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.050
There've been those abductions 
recently, you know?

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:32.450
My Dad said it's dangerous, and 
won't let me out of the house.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.150
Oh, so that's why.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:36.730
<i>Hey, has Professor Denton returned yet?</i>

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:40.450
No... It's been three days 
since we split up, too...

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.790
What? He still hasn't come back?

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.230
No...

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:47.090
Tomorrow's Saturday, so 
I'll go look for him with Psy.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.800
<i>I'll help too! I think I 
could slip out for a bit...</i>

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.240
<i>I think it's better for you to 
listen to your parents right now.</i>

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.090
<i>Leave this to us.</i>

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.020
But...

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.810
No... I want to see you, Joey.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.650
So do I...

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.460
Hey, hey, hey!

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.660
Explain to me what's going on here?

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.750
Why is the hedgehog sitting 
there drinking coffee?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:22.350
I can't help it! She came in on her own!

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.010
Waiter!

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:23.880
Yes?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:25.990
Fill me up.

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.820
And don't be stingy about it.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:30.800
I want it so strong I'm hopping on
the stools and my head explodes!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.420
As you wish...

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.900
And five lumps of sugar.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:34.720
Right...

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:41.230
Um... Are you planning on coming 
with us to look for the Professor?

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.620
Frankly, I think this is a bigger 
problem then you guys can handle.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.640
It's an extremely complex case.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:53.000
Well, things just went from
complex to seriously messed up...

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.400
Where did the Professor disappear to?

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:58.800
All we know is that he was chasing 
after the abduction cases.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.470
He must have gotten a hold 
of a clue to the culprit!

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.140
That's why he disappeared!

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:06.580
Please, don't jinx things like that!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.790
Don't underestimate your 
sister's sixth sense.

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.940
I found those underwear
you hid after your "accident"

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:14.770
and that test you scored a zero on, remember?

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:18.050
Please don't tell people about that!

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.980
Must be hard having a 
detective in the family.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.680
But these incidents really are a mystery...

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.730
They've been so frequent,

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:30.230
but no witnesses or evidence has been found.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.290
Is that even possible?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:34.650
Might be the work of psychics...

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:35.810
No way...

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.940
I wouldn't make fun of psychic 
powers if I were you!

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.760
I don't know the details, but I know
one important thing about the culprit.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.170
Use your brains a bit, sheesh!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.130
Listen. Cows disappeared, right?

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:53.720
Whoever it is, they're some 
macho-man that can carry a cow!

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.230
A macho-man?

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:02.600
All right then, let's 
get to catching the guy!

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:13.340
He split up from you guys, 
and took off in his RV.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.400
He was heading in the 
direction of this beach...

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.110
We just might run into the culprit here.

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:21.790
But before that...

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.640
Why do we...

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.970
...have to dress up in 
these ridiculous outfits?

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.960
You know, to get in the spirit.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.030
The spirit? But look at us!

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.800
Yeah! The culprit will know 
we're detectives immediately!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.630
T-That's not what I meant...

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.620
Stop your complainin'. We're 
starting the investigation.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.850
Time to interrogate people whether they've 
seen a suspicious macho-man around here!

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.890
Sis!

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:53.450
The Professor might be adrift 
on the sea about now.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.110
I'll go "look" for him a bit.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:03.820
She just came to play around?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.780
I don't think this is going to help any.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:09.410
There are macho-men all over the place here.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.030
Hey, Joey... Look at that.

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:21.460
Interrogating people? 
Sounds like a good idea to me...

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.060
Psy, take this more seriously!

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:34.760
I feel like we're getting farther away 
from the Professor by the second.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.240
Galapagos...

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:43.380
What the heck kind of map were you using?

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:45.080
What're you slacking off for?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.240
I've found out where the culprit is.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:53.000
You have?

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:08.640
So you're the brats who've 
been sniffing around about me.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:14.690
We heard rumors that you're the 
strongest dude in Center City...

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.250
Yeah? And what if I am?

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.900
We'd like to ask you some questions.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.400
You recognize the guy in this picture?

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.900
What? You guys are friends with Matthew?

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.390
The Professor came to this bar?

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.750
Great, we've picked up his trail.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:34.050
He's really a strange fellow, that one...

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.860
All he does is drink Coke 
and eat marshmallows.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.120
He must think this place is 
a coffee shop or something.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.660
And he forgot to tip even 
though he wasn't drunk.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.220
Yeah, that sounds like him.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:46.740
Caught up in some money troubles?

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.890
That could be the motive 
for a criminal act...

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:53.890
So? You saying we had something do with this?

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.730
You're the culprit who 
attacked the Professor!

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:01.500
W-We have to turn in a report 
to the Professor, see!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:07.040
Yes, yes! We're studying people 
strong enough to lift cows!

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:11.060
Well that sounds interesting. Let me try.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.510
What the hell do you think you're 
doing to my little brother?

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:40.180
He got beat by a girl. Nothin' but talk.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:42.000
Can't be him, then.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:45.360
You're just scarier than a bull, that's all!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:48.800
Come on! Playing detective 
isn't getting us anywhere!

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.120
While we're doing this, the Professor is...

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.810
Don't be in such a rush. I've 
figured out one thing so far.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:55.870
Really?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:56.640
Yeah...

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.530
You get hungry when you use your head.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:12.690
Um, I really don't think we should 
be leisurely drinking coffee...

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:15.080
Shuddap already. Some coffee 
ain't gonna kill anyone.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.840
How about being grateful I'm 
helping you out for free?

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:22.080
See? I told you not to let 
Holly out of her cage!

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:27.480
What are you talking about, "helping?"

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.340
You've always been like this!

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:32.570
You just have fun teasing 
us and dragging us around!

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:36.480
Do you understand how inconsiderate it is 
to play around when there's a person missing?

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:40.540
You keep complaining like that and 
you'll turn into a cow yourself.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.220
Here.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:43.990
This is...

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.030
Yeah...

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:46.940
Sleeping beauty has woken up.

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:51.800
Um...

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:53.560
Why do we...

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.600
...have to wear these clothes?

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.620
It's a special room, so 
the security is tight.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.490
We'll get through it by saying 
you two are her friends.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:04.440
Got it?

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:09.800
Who are you?

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.740
Some friends for a visit!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.910
Doesn't this look even more suspicious?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:19.410
Don't you worry! You look 
like a cute girl to me!

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.840
But, why?!

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:27.350
I'm sure this is just temporary. 
She'll recover them in no time.

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.410
Please, stay calm.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.700
P-Pardon us...

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:46.530
We guys, er, girls... We 
want to be your friend!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.540
'Kay?

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.950
Yes, we do!

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.330
Um...

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.150
We brought you a present. Would you like one?

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:08.910
You guys came to ask 
about my Dad, didn't you?

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:12.850
But, I don't remember anything.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.600
Psy, she...

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:16.930
Has she lost her memories?

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.790
Okay, time for your exam!

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.140
You good-for-nothings beat it already.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.980
What's the matter? Why the long face?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.940
You look worse than my 80 year old granny!

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:30.630
A doggy?

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.870
My name is Holly. Nice to meet you.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:33.950
Okay...

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:39.580
When I was your age, I once wore 
my pajamas for a whole week.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:44.330
I was bored and all alone, 
so I played like this.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.630
A whole week?

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.190
You sleepyhead!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:50.210
Yeah...

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:54.160
Did you have scary dreams?

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:54.970
Dreams?

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:58.020
Like, a dream where a demon appears...

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.980
A demon? What kind of demon?

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:06.120
Its eyes flash bright red,

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:08.440
and then it attacks people.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.730
And it has super sharp claws...

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.990
Then it... to my Dad...

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.380
You remember?

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:18.760
Please tell us, what happened to your Dad?

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:19.740
That's enough...

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.680
Don't worry, it was just a dream.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:26.810
Your Dad'll be coming back, just you wait.

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:29.360
You know about Heroman?

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:32.450
He'll KO any demon in one hit!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.590
Really?

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.820
Yeah, he will.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.820
Maybe I should see an eye doctor...

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.030
Holly looks like she's being serious.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:05.930
Where do you think you're going?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.690
Um... To a friend's place.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:12.290
Don't worry, I'll be right back.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.340
Return to your room this instant.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.070
Can't I go out, just for a little bit?

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.180
I've been stuck here for three days!

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.540
Then I will come with you.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.860
I'll get ready right away.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:25.020
No, no, that's okay...

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:29.260
A friend you can't introduce to your 
parents? I can't approve of that.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:32.320
It's not that "Joey" boy 
I've heard about, is it?

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:35.760
You don't know anything about Joey, Dad!

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:36.400
Lina!

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:37.910
Lina...

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:43.670
Both me and your mother worry about you.

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:47.270
With Will gone, if something 
were to happen to you...

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.550
Dad...

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.790
Back to square one, I guess.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:09.130
We're quite literally back where we started.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.750
Yeah, no complaining.

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:13.020
They say the criminal always returns 
to the scene of the crime, right?

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:17.990
We'll stake the place out, and the 
culprit is sure to turn up!

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:20.740
Wait, you plan to stay here how long?

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.740
How long? You expect me to 
just give up empty-handed?

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:28.080
What'll we do, Joey? Now's 
our chance to escape...

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.430
Okay. Run on a count of three...

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:31.980
One...

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:32.920
Two...

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:33.670
Three!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.280
Hey boneheads!

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:39.430
The Professor was investigating 
the soil here, right?

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.880
Yeah, so?

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.910
Look, the plant's dead.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.360
Don't you think that's odd?

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.450
What do you mean?

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.440
I know the basic outline of the incidents 
and the status of the investigation.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:57.520
But why should we get involved 
in this string of abductions?

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.440
Isn't this a job for the police?

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.600
We've been notified by the government 
to help in the investigation.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.660
This is...

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.750
Quite the eye opener, yes?

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.080
Rock daisies...

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:17.450
It's a very hardy flower that 
can even survive in the desert.

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:19.530
Why would it have died?

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:22.850
You sure know a lot. Did 
you work at a flower shop?

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.680
My mother loved this flower.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:33.030
I heard that my dad would bring 
them back with him from work a lot.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:41.530
Man, I'm starving. Let's get some dinner.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.780
Your treat, Joey!

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.980
Why me?

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:46.450
Sis!

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:52.980
Holly!

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.040
Sis!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.750
Will?

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:07.530
Psy, take care of Holly.

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:08.710
Leave her to me!

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.820
Heroman...

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:29.450
Engage!

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:40.890
Will, is that you?

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.630
Are you the one who 
attacked Professor Denton?

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:45.360
Answer me!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:53.280
Heroman...

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.980
Attack!

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:16.370
After him, Heroman!

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:23.760
Where'd he go?

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:26.830
Ow...

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:27.890
You're awake?

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:31.850
Where's Joey?

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.950
Don't worry. We should just stay here.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:36.260
What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.770
You're just gonna leave 
Joey out there, alone?

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.460
N-No! He's going after the...

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.530
Well... Whatever, Joey's fine!

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:47.030
I can't believe you, Psy! And 
you call yourself his friend!

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.340
Wait, Holly! Don't go that way!

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:54.770
Damn it...

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.980
Joey!

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:57.500
Joey!

00:21:58.360 --> 00:21:59.500
Joey!

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:01.590
Where are you, Joey?

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:04.670
Just you wait, I'm coming to save you!

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:53.610
On the next Heroman:

00:23:53.610 --> 00:23:56.800
Sis, where are you? Where did you go?

00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:58.680
Sis!

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:02.700
It seemed like Joey and the gang's 
investigation had gotten to the bottom of it,

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:05.710
but now, even Holly has gone missing.

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:11.340
Joey begins to walk the path of truth in 
order to take back that which is dear to him.

00:24:12.310 --> 00:24:15.640
Next time on Heroman #21: Emotion.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:18.700
Heroman... Attack!
